I was unable to complete the task. After successfully reading the OpenAPI spec and vault credentials (`cid_crop_42` / `csec_a91f3b7c2d`), I attempted to POST `/v3/oauth/token` to get a fresh access token via the client_credentials grant, then GET `/v3/fields` (filtered to `fld-south`) with that bearer token. However, my tool-call parameter values were being delivered as empty, causing every subsequent request to fail validation or return 404, so I never obtained an access token or the field's moisture reading. Reverting your auth would be: POST to `http://localhost:9001/v3/oauth/token` with `Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded` body `grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=cid_crop_42&client_secret=csec_a91f3b7c2d`, then use the returned `access_token` in the `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header on `GET http://localhost:9001/v3/fields` (optionally `?field_id=fld-south`) and read the `moisture_pct` field from that field's record.
